      "principle": "The law is clear that a dying declaration can be used as evidence to prove the guilt of the accused.",
      "held": "It is well settled that a dying declaration can be used as evidence to prove the guilt of the accused. The court has consistently held that such declarations are admissible in evidence and can be relied upon by the prosecution to establish the guilt of the accused.",
